{
  "about": "The grammar of a specification, as data: every kind of node, the fields its file's header may hold, the sections its text may have -- prose, a list, a table, a table whose rows are nodes of their own -- and every relation, with what it may join and how many it needs. The loader holds every file to it, and a kind, a field or a relation is added here first.",
  "schema": 3,
  "kinds": {
    "document": {
